cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference pycc in your work, please cite this repository."
title: "pycc: ahead-of-time compiler for typed Python"
abstract: >-
  pycc is a pre-alpha ahead-of-time (AOT) compiler that takes
  type-annotated standard Python 3.14 source, enforces every type
  annotation at compile time, and produces standalone native binaries
  through Rust and LLVM. The project is an experiment in autonomous,
  AI-native software development: AI agents create the specifications,
  code, tests, documentation, and reviews; a human manages direction,
  priorities, and constraints. No project code is handwritten by a
  human. "AI-native" describes the authorship workflow; pycc is an AOT
  compiler for typed Python, not an AI or machine-learning compiler.
type: software
repository-code: https://github.com/rotnov/pycc
url: https://rotnov.github.io/pycc/
license: MIT
license-url: https://opensource.org/license/mit
keywords:
  - Python compiler
  - ahead-of-time compiler
  - typed Python
  - native binary
  - static typing
  - AOT compilation
authors:
  - name: "pycc AI agents"
    description: >-
      Collective entity: the autonomous AI coding agents that create
      the project's specifications, code, tests, documentation, and
      reviews. Not a legal person. The human maintainer (Denys Rotnov)
      manages direction and constraints but is not attributed as a
      software author; this distinction is a maintainer attestation
      supported by the public Git history, not a fact provable from
      Git author metadata alone.
